//? Title: Flashsort: actual value classes, carried cycles and the insertion tail
//? Subtitle: Checked arithmetic, original samples and measured work under matched occupancies
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given finite numeric values, produce an ascending ordering while preserving every element.
Value ranges can suggest a useful partial ordering before many comparisons are made.
Flashsort maps values into ordered classes, carries values into their class ranges, and
finishes with insertion sort. This report inspects native carry records, preserves the
original fifteen-value and 2,000-sample examples, and measures the actual classes and
finishing work. Equal class occupancies can still lead to very different insertion costs;
the class vector also takes linear auxiliary storage for this implementation's default.
)

\toc

> The method: class ranges turn values into destinations

For n>1 nonconstant values, the implementation chooses m=max(2,int(0.43n)) classes.
In exact arithmetic, the linear classification is

$$
k(v)=\left\lfloor\frac{m-1}{v_{\max}-v_{\min}}(v-v_{\min})\right\rfloor,
\qquad 0\le k(v)\le m-1.
$$
\alttext(The class is the floor of a value's normalised offset multiplied by one less than the number of classes.)

The native map retains the historical rounded double coefficient and multiplication order
when those operations are safe. Integral differences are computed in an unsigned domain
of the same width, without signed subtraction overflow. Extreme or tiny floating ranges
that make the historical expression unsafe use a scaled long-double ratio. The position
is clamped before conversion to an index. Boundary rounding is part of this finite map;
it need not equal an arbitrary-precision evaluation of the displayed formula.

Count each original class occupancy c_k and form exclusive ends E_k=sum_{r≤k}c_r.
Class k owns slots [E_{k−1},E_k), with E_{−1}=0. The mutable boundary vector L starts at E.
A carried value of class k goes to slot --L_k; the displaced value becomes the next carry.
When a cycle closes, scanning for the next unfilled leader continues to the right.
Each destination is consumed at most once. The native variant retains its original
cycle order and does not first swap the maximum to position zero.

> Three values: follow every carried exchange

For [2,0,1], m=2 and k(v)=floor(v/2): values 0 and 1 belong to class 0, while 2 belongs
to class 1. Counts are [2,1], so the initial exclusive ends are [2,3]. Start by carrying
value 2 from slot zero. Its destination is --L_1=2, displacing 1. Then 1 goes to
--L_0=1, displacing 0. Finally 0 goes to --L_0=0 and the cycle closes.
The array is [0,1,2]; insertion sort has nothing to shift.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flash_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <climits>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
const auto t=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<int>{2,0,1});
  std::print("Original assignments: {}; counts {}; exclusive ends {}.\n\n",t.class_of_input,t.class_counts,t.class_ends);
  std::print("| cycle start | class | destination | carried value | displaced value |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto&r:t.moves)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",r.cycle_start,r.class_index,r.destination,r.carried,r.displaced);
  std::print("\nActual grouped state {}; output {}; carry writes {}; insertion shifts {}.\n",t.classified,t.output,t.work.permutation_writes,t.work.insertion_shifts);
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle b;b.width=3.6;b.height=1.9;b.font_size=23;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.moves.size();++i){const auto&r=t.moves[i];g.node(std::to_string(i),{5.4*i,0},std::format("Write {} to slot {}\nClass {}\nCarry becomes {}",r.carried,r.destination,r.class_index,r.displaced),b);if(i)g.edge(std::to_string(i-1),std::to_string(i));}
  g.text({5.4,2.5},"Class 0 owns [0,2); class 1 owns [2,3)",25).text({5.4,-2.5},"The third exchange closes the cycle at slot zero",25).text({5.4,-3.9},"Grouped and sorted state: 0 1 2",24).save_svg("build/flash_tiny.svg");
  if(t.moves.size()!=3||t.output!=std::vector<int>{0,1,2})throw std::runtime_error("tiny carry identity");
}
```
