\alttext(A native three-node carry diagram writes value two to slot two, value one to slot one and value zero to slot zero. It labels the two class ranges and the completed cycle.)

> Class ordered does not mean fully sorted

For [4,1,3,0,2], m=2 again. Class 0 contains four values and class 1 contains only the
maximum. The native carry phase produces [1,3,0,2,4]. Every value is in its class range,
but three strict inversions remain: (1,0), (3,0) and (3,2). The insertion tail must remove
those three inversions, one predecessor shift at a time. Equal keys are not shifted by
insertion, but the preceding nonadjacent cycle exchanges give no stability guarantee.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flash_tail.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <climits>
