> Checked full ranges and complete owned evidence

The old template formed max−min in the input type. INT_MAX−INT_MIN overflowed signed
int before conversion. Finite floating inputs could also overflow their range or produce
an infinite coefficient on a tiny range, followed by an invalid integer cast. Bounded
sanitizer probes reproduce those failures in the frozen original. The checked map keeps
ordinary safe results and carries intact while handling those full ranges safely.

Floating inputs must all be finite, including a singleton. Invalid data is rejected before
mutation; n must fit the legacy int index domain. The vector signature and existing
sorting_extra.hpp include remain available. The implementation supports arithmetic types
other than bool; it is not a generic comparator or payload-key sorting interface.

The optional trace validates and scans extrema once, then checks complete capture C=5n+2m
before copying or sorting. Shortcuts use C=2n and have no class arrays or carry history.
The default entry cap is one million; zero disables only that optional cap. Owned records
are independent copies, and failure returns no partial trace. Ordinary in-place sorting
and work counters do not allocate history or impose that optional quota.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flash_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <climits>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
const auto integers=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<int>{INT_MIN,0,INT_MAX});
  const double hi=std::numeric_limits<double>::max(),lo=std::numeric_limits<double>::denorm_min();
  const auto wide=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<double>{-hi,0,hi});const auto tiny=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<double>{0,lo,2*lo});
  std::print("Full int range sorted: {}; assignments {}.\n",integers.output,integers.class_of_input);
  std::print("Finite double extremes: sorted {}; scaled fallback {}; assignments {}.\n",std::is_sorted(wide.output.begin(),wide.output.end()),wide.work.scaled_classification,wide.class_of_input);
  std::print("Positive subnormal range: sorted {}; scaled fallback {}; assignments {}.\n",std::is_sorted(tiny.output.begin(),tiny.output.end()),tiny.work.scaled_classification,tiny.class_of_input);
  bool invalid=false;std::vector<double>bad{3,std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),1};try{dm::algorithms::flashsort(bad);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid=true;}
  bool capacity=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::flashsort_class_count(static_cast<std::size_t>(INT_MAX)+1);}catch(const std::length_error&){capacity=true;}
  bool under=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<int>{2,0,1},18);}catch(const std::length_error&){under=true;}
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<int>{2,0,1},19),uncapped=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<int>{2,0,1},0);auto edited=exact;edited.input[0]=99;edited.classified[0]=99;edited.output[0]=99;edited.moves[0].carried=99;
  std::print("Nonfinite input rejected before mutation {}; virtual oversized length rejected {}.\n",invalid&&bad[0]==3&&std::isnan(bad[1])&&bad[2]==1,capacity);
  std::print("Complete trace: cap19 succeeds; cap18 rejects {}; disabled cap agrees {}; retained output {}; edited first output {}.\n",under,uncapped.output==exact.output,exact.output,edited.output[0]);
  const auto constant=dm::algorithms::flashsort_trace(std::vector<int>{7,7,7},6);
  std::print("Constant shortcut: classes {}; carry records {}; insertion shifts {}; capture bound 6 entries.\n",constant.work.class_count,constant.moves.size(),constant.work.insertion_shifts);
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(60,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle b;b.width=3.8;b.height=2;b.font_size=23;
  g.node("input",{0,0},"Validate finite data\nCheck signed length\nScan extrema once",b).node("map",{5.6,0},"Safe class map\nFull integer spans\nScaled float fallback",b).node("sort",{11.2,0},"Shared carry loop\nInsertion tail\nOwned optional trace",b).edge("input","map").edge("map","sort").text({5.6,-2.7},"Complete capture is admitted before copying and sorting",24).save_svg("build/flash_controls.svg");
  if(!invalid||!capacity||!under||wide.work.scaled_classification!=true||tiny.work.scaled_classification!=true)throw std::runtime_error("checked controls");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full int range sorted: [-2147483648, 0, 2147483647]; assignments [0, 0, 1].
Finite double extremes: sorted true; scaled fallback true; assignments [0, 0, 1].
Positive subnormal range: sorted true; scaled fallback true; assignments [0, 0, 1].
